  "note": "Subrata Dey, the lane caretaker, lives in location.nabapara.caretaker_flat (his home). Every day he sleeps from 21:30 to 05:15 and has breakfast at home. On Monday to Saturday he walks the lane (06:15-07:00, location.nabapara.lane_round, an authored off-lane leg) and checks the shared entry of the tall flats (07:16-08:00, anchor.tall_flats.front_door). On Monday to Friday he then sweeps the stair (08:08-08:40) and works at the noticeboard (08:44-09:13); on Saturday he goes straight to the noticeboard (08:04-08:40). He is home for the midday meal and rest from 09:50 (Saturday 09:17, Sunday 09:36) and stays home until the afternoon: at home through 13:00-14:00 reading, on Monday to Friday he walks back to check the entry (14:33-15:00), attends to the stair (15:08-15:50) and works at the noticeboard again (15:54-16:53), then walks home (arrives 17:30). Saturday and Sunday afternoons are spent at home. Every evening he is home from 17:30 (supper, then reading) until 20:30; Monday to Saturday he then does a short evening round of the lane (20:48-21:12) and is home again at 21:30, asleep; Sunday he rests at home from 20:30. Because he is home at every minute from 10:00 to 12:30 and from 17:30 to 20:30 on every day of the week, the caretaker flat's visiting hours (Doors.cpp: 10:00-12:30 and 17:30-20:30) are always answered by a host who is awake. The anchors in the tall flats are the shared stair/entry (door.nabapara.tall_flats_front is public). The lane-round and walking legs are authored off-lane lengths; the tall-flats legs are conservative ceilings over the built shared-entry passage until the presenter bindings exist. Every travel duration is ceil(sum(lengthCm)/140).",
